    {"claim": "The biggest risk to this MVP isn't bad code — it's not shipping.", "targets": []},
    {"claim": "Human developers are already the dominant source of technical debt in every established codebase — developers spend roughly 33% of their time dealing with technical debt authored entirely by humans.", "targets": []},
    {"claim": "Allocate 5–7% of your 90-day sprint capacity to automated test generation, real-time error telemetry, and rollback triggers — that costs roughly 4–6 engineering days, versus a two-week upfront audit that consumes 15% of your timeline.", "targets": []},
    {"claim": "The terminal maintenance burden scenario requires a specific organizational failure identical whether a human or an AI wrote the code — the fix is iteration discipline, not authorship policing.", "targets": []},
    {"claim": "AI-generated prototype code converts to validated learning the moment real users touch it; the only thing that converts it to terminal burden is a team that stops iterating.", "targets": []}
  ]
}
