sts by 2-5x when those prototypes must connect to real infrastructure.\n\nSo here's the question nobody in the room wants to answer honestly. If AI-generated code is such a clear accelerant, why does the entire case for it depend on a 90-day measurement window? Who chose that window? Who benefits from stopping the clock before the maintenance invoices arrive? The Accelerationist says terminal maintenance burden only happens if you stop iterating. Fine. But you're iterating on code you don't understand, written by a system that can't explain its choices, integrated into an architecture whose implicit contracts were never documented because the humans who built it carried that knowledge in their heads. What does the 180-day cost curve look like? What does the 360-day attrition rate look like for the engineers who spent their year babysitting AI output instead of building? Show me those numbers. Because right now, the entire case for AI-generated MVPs in established companies is built on a ledger that only counts one side of the transaction.",
